<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῠφελ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
			A.R.
			2.323
		</span></i>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pers.</u>
			965
		</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
			Parth.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			29.4
		</span></i>, etc.:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard,
				rough</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στυφελοῦ . . ἐπ᾽ ἀκτᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. (lyr.); in later Poets, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτὴ
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκόπελος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.31
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.442
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of flavour,
				<i>astringent, sour, acid</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					4.1.22
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταγών</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.561
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph.,
				<i>harsh, severe, cruel</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφέται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					79
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόλχοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					1012
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στυφελός</span> was a Clitorian
			word for <i>hard. rough</i>, and used at Cyrene for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέρσος</span>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Zenod.
			</span></i> ap. Sch. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1005
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
